                <pb facs="0688" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.6331/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stockton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-27T17:00:00-05:00">March 27, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Legation’s 21. March 26, 5 p.m. To date we are without a text of the
                    agreement on the proposed customs union. The statement in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Presse</hi> attributed to the Commerce Department is
                    denied here by the responsible officials. Moreover, we are not seeking
                    explanations either from Germany or Austria. Under these circumstances, if the
                    Austrian Government raises the question, you may, at your discretion, informally
                    review the situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
